# vShowroom — cross-institutional artefact brief

> **L3 · Product logic.** Distinct from teaching (L1) and research (L2) — see [`fe-unit-forge.mdc`](./fe-unit-forge.mdc) §0. This document specifies *the thing being built*. It is not a syllabus and not a grade.

---

## 1. The synergy is already in both official guides

This is not an invented crossover. Both subjects' official `contents` require it:

| | **Creación Digital I–II** (Universidad Europea) | **Front-End I–II** (UDIT) |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Degree | Grado en **Comunicación y Gestión de Moda** | Desarrollo Full-Stack · Ciencia de Datos e IA |
| Placement | **Year 1** — S1 and S2 · 6 ECTS each | FE I **Year 2 annual**; FE II **Year 3 S1** · 6 ECTS each |
| Relevant official contents | CD I: *"Fundamentos y representación de la forma tridimensional. Volumen."* · CD II: **"Creación de avatares"**, **"Diseño de experiencias de moda digitales"**, **"Maquetación, edición y creación de web y portfolio digital"**, **"Hologramas y R.A"** | FE II: arquitecturas, PWA, testing, rendimiento, **R3F/WebGL**, **shaders**, **IoT/servicios Python** |

**CD II is officially required to produce web and digital portfolio work, and 3D avatars, and AR.** FE II is officially required to teach 3D interfaces on the web. The two curricula already point at the same artefact from opposite sides. The synergy makes each subject *more* compliant with its own guide, not less.

**One professor, two institutions, one methodology:** the same critical, AI-assisted, docs-first paradigm — *another way of the tao, but the tao is one and many*.

