## 4. Semester choreography — the hard constraint

The calendars do **not** align for live co-teaching:

```
        S1 (Sep–Jan)                    S2 (Feb–Jun)
UDIT    FE II  ██████ builds platform
        FE I   ████████████████████████████████████ (annual — the bridge)
UEM     CD I   ██████ 2D/3D foundations
                                        CD II ██████ avatars · web portfolio · AR
```

**Therefore: asynchronous handoff, not synchronous collaboration.**

| Window | Who | Does |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **S1** | FE II | Builds and releases vShowroom **v1** against *seed* content |
| **S1→S2 boundary** | — | **Handoff:** tagged release, deployed URL, contribution guide, open issues |
| **S2** | CD II | Populates with real avatars/designs; **files issues as users**, not as clients |
| **S2** | FE I | Maintains and extends; consumes CD II's issues as authentic backlog |

> **Why this is better than co-teaching:** CD II students become **real users with real content**, and FE I inherits a **live product with real bug reports** — which no invented brief can manufacture. The temporal offset is a feature.

**Seed content for S1:** FE II cannot wait for CD II. Use openly-licensed 3D garment assets or the professor's own, clearly labelled as seed, replaced in S2.

