## 5. Consent and rights — this is where a fashion crossover gets dangerous

Student design work is **authored creative property**. Nothing here is covered by the FE consent set.

| # | Consent | Whose | Nature |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **S1** | Exhibiting a design in vShowroom | CD student | Per-artefact, revocable, licence stated (author retains copyright; platform gets display licence only) |
| **S2** | Attribution vs. anonymity | CD student | Author's choice; default is attributed, but opt-out must exist |
| **S3** | Research use of the interaction data | both cohorts | Separate from S1/S2; per [`fe-cohort-case-proposal.mdc`](./fe-cohort-case-proposal.mdc) §6 |
| **S4** | Cross-institution data flow | UDIT ↔ UEM | **Two institutions, two regimes.** Needs both DPOs. Minimise: the platform should hold no personal data of visitors in v1 |

**Design rule that avoids most of the problem:** v1 stores *pieces and designers*, and "collect/follow" state stays **client-side (localStorage)** unless and until accounts are justified. No accounts, no visitor personal data, no cross-border transfer question.

> If the DPO conversation stalls, **ship v1 with local-only collections.** The product still works and the research still has cohort-level engineering evidence.

---

## 6. What each side gets

**FE students** — a real client with real content, a genuine performance problem (3D assets are heavy), an accessibility problem that matters (can a screen-reader user navigate a 3D showroom?), and a public artefact for their portfolio.

**CD students** — their work exhibited on a platform built to professional standards, and a first encounter with the interface layer as something *made*, not given.

**The professor** — one methodology, two subjects, two institutions, and a single artefact that is simultaneously the teaching deliverable, the research object, and the open-education asset (OEGlobal-nominable, see the proposal §7).

**The fields** — a documented attempt at the fashion-portfolio framework gap, from a cohort that has both halves.

---

## 7. Risks

| Risk | Mitigation |
| --- | --- |
| Two institutions, two ethics regimes | Start the DPO conversation at both **before September**; design v1 to need as little as possible (§5) |
| CD II content arrives after FE II ends | That is the design (§4), not a failure — seed content in S1 |
| Scope inflation ("add try-on!") | §3 out-of-scope list is binding; VTON is an open research problem, not a student sprint |
| One repo, n<15, uneven contribution | Rotating roles + individual exercise channel (forge §2) + oral defence |
| Fashion students' work misused | §5 consents; author retains copyright; revocable |
| Professor bandwidth across two universities | The artefact is **one** product, not two. That is the whole point of the synergy |
